  "content": {
    "id": "p32-q5-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "5",
    "prompt": "Suppose $\\triangle ABC$ has vertices $A(6,2)$, $B(5,4)$ and $C(3,6)$. Find the exact length of each side, and the measure of each angle, correct to the nearest degree.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": {
        "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
        "version": 1,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "id": "p32-q5-short-results",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "AB=\\sqrt5,\\quad BC=2\\sqrt2,\\quad CA=5",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "break"
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "\\angle A=10^\\circ,\\quad\\angle B=162^\\circ,\\quad\\angle C=8^\\circ",
                "display": false
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "p32-q5-short-method",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Use the distance formula for the sides, then the cosine rule for the angles.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "Using the distance formula,\n$$\\begin{align*}AB&=\\sqrt{(5-6)^2+(4-2)^2}\\\\AB&=\\sqrt5\\\\BC&=\\sqrt{(3-5)^2+(6-4)^2}\\\\BC&=\\sqrt8=2\\sqrt2\\\\CA&=\\sqrt{(6-3)^2+(2-6)^2}\\\\CA&=5.\\end{align*}$$\nUsing the cosine rule,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\cos A&=\\frac{AB^2+CA^2-BC^2}{2(AB)(CA)}\\\\\\cos A&=\\frac{5+25-8}{2\\sqrt5\\times5}\\\\\\cos A&=\\frac{11}{5\\sqrt5}\\\\A&=\\cos^{-1}\\left(\\frac{11}{5\\sqrt5}\\right)\\\\A&\\approx10^\\circ.\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}\\cos B&=\\frac{AB^2+BC^2-CA^2}{2(AB)(BC)}\\\\\\cos B&=\\frac{5+8-25}{2\\sqrt5\\times2\\sqrt2}\\\\\\cos B&=-\\frac3{\\sqrt{10}}\\\\B&=\\cos^{-1}\\left(-\\frac3{\\sqrt{10}}\\right)\\\\B&\\approx162^\\circ.\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}\\cos C&=\\frac{BC^2+CA^2-AB^2}{2(BC)(CA)}\\\\\\cos C&=\\frac{8+25-5}{2\\times2\\sqrt2\\times5}\\\\\\cos C&=\\frac7{5\\sqrt2}\\\\C&=\\cos^{-1}\\left(\\frac7{5\\sqrt2}\\right)\\\\C&\\approx8^\\circ.\\end{align*}$$\nThe rounded angles sum to $180^\\circ$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 100
  },
